WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.217 --> 00:00:01.800
RETO MEIER: It's
officially week eight

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.780
of Google Cloud Next
on Air, which means

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.813
we're focusing on Cloud AI.

00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:07.980
I'm Reto Meier, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud,"

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.550
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.740
Week eight is all
about Cloud AI,

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.440
meaning we want you to see
how AI can help everyone

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.623
on your team.

00:00:17.623 --> 00:00:20.040
There's all kinds of talks
this week that cover everything

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.910
from infrastructure to
train AI and ML projects all

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.660
the way to managed
offerings that give you

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.400
the benefits of
ML without having

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.880
to train your own models.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.430
So check out all
the talks this week

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.320
and add interesting
sessions to your playlist

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.730
so you can watch them on demand.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.760
And speaking of
managed offerings,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.470
this week, we're
shining the spotlight

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.980
on measuring and improving
speech-to-text accuracy.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.530
While the speech-to-text API is
already great out of the box,

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.560
you may have custom needs for
your industry or use case.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.170
So this talk walks
you through how

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.400
you can customize your
model, improve accuracy,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.400
and even features a lab
where you can try it out

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.930
for yourself.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.910
One session I'm
super excited for

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.390
is Interpreting ML Models
with Explainable AI.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.580
No matter what the
accuracy of your ML model,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.709
it can be hard to
know exactly how it

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:06.420
comes to that prediction.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.580
Thankfully, this talk
covers Explainable AI,

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.470
which puts the
tools in your hands

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.560
to help you increase your
model's transparency.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.650
If you want to learn how to
use Explainable AI and the What

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.660
If tool to better
understand your models,

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.150
make sure to add this
one to your playlist.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.520
Finally, have you had a
chance to check out Kaggle?

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.070
It's a fully customizable
notebook environment

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.022
where you can get access to
all the code and data you need,

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:31.230
as well as access all sorts
of learning opportunities

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.880
and competitions.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.680
This week also
features a session

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.800
talking about how Kaggle
transitioned from GPUs to TPUs,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.280
so check out that talk
and get hands-on with ML.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.410
To add these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.860
check out the link.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.740
Any thoughts or ideas,
leave us a comment

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.890
or tweet us using the
hashtag #GoogleCloudNext.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.700
We'll see you in the cloud.

